[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2332966062","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/587#issuecomment-2332966062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/587","id":2332966062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6LDjyu","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-06T00:40:10Z","updated_at":"2024-09-06T00:40:10Z","body":"Strings aren't supported for the render prop, it's: `render={<div />}`. However, it still doesn't select since it relies on the `label` `for` prop to select the control. This is similar to native `button` components allowing you to compose non-native buttons which will need to switch to the `useButton` hook to work. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2332966062/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2344367584","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/587#issuecomment-2344367584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/587","id":2344367584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6LvDXg","user":{"login":"oliviertassinari","id":3165635,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjU2MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3165635?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari","html_url":"https://github.com/oliviertassinari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-11T18:16:08Z","updated_at":"2024-09-12T18:11:53Z","body":"> This is similar to native button components allowing you to compose non-native buttons which will need to switch to the useButton hook to work.\r\n\r\nI love that feature: same look & feel, different behavior.\r\n\r\n> Strings aren't supported for the render prop, it's: `render={<div />}`. However, it still doesn't select since it relies on the label for prop to select the control.\r\n\r\nI'm confused then, I would imagine that we have possible paths:\r\n\r\n1. `render` prop is not supported (it doesn't work today)\r\n2. we implement the mouse up to focus \r\n\r\nI was more coming from the angel of option 1.: what's the use case for allowing changing the slot on `Field.Label`? Now, let's say there is a valid use case, then why shouldn't it also move focus like the native one?\r\n\r\n> Strings aren't supported for the render prop, it's: `render={<div />}`\r\n\r\nAh ok, TypeScript is most of the time broken in CodeSandbox, so I tend to rely on the console log, but the logs said nothing was wrong 😄 .","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2344367584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2345211610","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/587#issuecomment-2345211610","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/587","id":2345211610,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6LyRba","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-12T03:49:11Z","updated_at":"2024-09-12T03:51:50Z","body":"The solution is to either:\r\n\r\n1. Remove the shorthand `render` prop for `Label` components and require that a `<label>` tag always gets rendered. The function version of the `render` prop errors in TypeScript since it uses `React.ComponentPropsWithRef<'label'>`, which errors when spreading those props on e.g. a `<div />`.\r\n2. Still allow shorthand `render` but add logic so that clicking the non-native label works like `for` does for `label`. Note: the `aria-labelledby` prop already exists so that focusable form controls are still linked.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2345211610/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2346941050","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/587#issuecomment-2346941050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/587","id":2346941050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6L43p6","user":{"login":"oliviertassinari","id":3165635,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjU2MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3165635?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari","html_url":"https://github.com/oliviertassinari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oliviertassinari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-12T18:11:09Z","updated_at":"2024-09-12T18:11:09Z","body":"@atomiks  If we assume that a label should always support mouseup focus associated input, then it makes sense to me, it's one of those two 👍 .\r\n\r\nIn case 1. I would be curious to understand when it's helpful to not render a `<label>`, to get the same level of clarity as the use case of `<Button render=\"<a>\">` (which seems clear).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2346941050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]]